  "id": "auditory-distance-perception",
  "term": "auditory distance perception",
  "definition": "Auditory distance perception is the ability to judge how far away a sound source is from oneself using hearing. Research in the packet indicates that these judgments are typically less accurate and more variable than visual distance judgments, and they improve when congruent visual information is available.",
